WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.820
I'm gonna wet my pants.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.830
Phone Duty - 
We Have an Emergency

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.120
"The mission to confirm maintenance,
to the HQ-command line,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.590
for high-level emergency situations."

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.010
Th-That's quite a name...

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.340
It's an extremely important mission.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.560
If we fail, we could
all be punished.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.980
Under certain conditions,
a level-one warning is issued,

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.840
and all forces in the area are placed
on emergency standby.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.660
That's right. It's really important.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.900
Wh-What kind of mission is it?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.660
You see...

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.490
You watch the phone.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:15.250
You know this phone is our hotline
to the capital's HQ, right?

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.310
Has it ever rung?

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.210
No.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.480
That's right.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.630
Thankfully.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.010
But maybe...

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.430
Yes, it would be bad if it rang,

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.680
but it would be even worse
if it didn't ring when it should.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.580
So once every six months,
they test to ensure it works.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.460
And we call that...

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.020
Well...

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.550
Remember it, already.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.900
The command communications line
for high-level... What was it?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.080
No... It's the command communications
line for the high-level...

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.620
The mission to confirm maintenance,
to the HQ command line

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.650
for high-level emergency situations.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.000
Exactly.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.720
Yes, yes, yes, <i>yes!</i>

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.360
Please let me do it!

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.220
I've always wanted to try
talking on the telephone!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.300
Is it that exciting?

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.790
It works in more or less the same way
as the Takemikazuchi's intercom.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.690
It's just that the distance
is a bit further.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.510
But it's amazing.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.960
You can talk to people
really far away!

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:18.820
It's wonderful.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:25.550
Well, it's kind of strange to talk
to someone you can't see.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.080
But once you get used
to it, it's nothing.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:32.740
But the issue is that we don't know
when it'll happen today.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.080
You still want to do it?

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.460
Of course!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.960
OK.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.460
Then, you watch the phone
the entire day.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.470
Ring, ring, ring!

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:53.260
This is Private Sorami Kanata of the
1121 Platoon, Helvetian Republic Army.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:00.340
And when the call ends,
you replace the receiver on top.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.290
OK!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.940
Fi-Fi...

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.410
You're so cute!

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:48.940
Filicia-san!

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.860
What are you doing?

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.200
It hurts to watch.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:54.300
The train's leaving.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.330
Train?

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.610
I need to rush some
documents to HQ.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.480
Claus-san comes next
week, right?

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.340
So I'm off to the station.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.400
Take care of the phone, OK?

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.050
Right!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:14.190
If we don't do it right, they might think
we've actually been attacked.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.430
Don't screw it up!

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.500
Leave it to me!

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.670
Hey!

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.250
Yes?

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.310
I'm not asleep!

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.170
Not... Not asleep at all!

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.100
Have you seen Noël?

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.790
She wasn't in her room.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.240
Um...

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.980
The hanger again?

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:55.670
OK...

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:58.780
Kanata, what do you
want for lunch?

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.050
I-I-I'll get it.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.310
Don't worry about it.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.440
It's my turn.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:04.190
But...

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:07.060
Why do both you and Kureha

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:11.480
try to keep me from the kitchen,
even when it's my turn?

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:15.450
I used to cook all the time
before you two came.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.710
Well, you see...

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.500
It should taste fine.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.790
I-It doesn't taste as
bad as it looks...

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.370
What?

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.010
Wait, it's got a very strong
taste! It's wonderful!

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.850
Doesn't it?

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:34.260
Then I'll go at it even
harder than usual.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.770
Hey! Is anyone here?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.400
Yes!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.840
Sempai, it's Naomi-san!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.270
I'm busy.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:49.580
But I need to stay by the phone!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.960
Hey, you've got a visitor!

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.790
Darn it! Fine.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.790
OK, I'll be right there.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:06.150
I don't want any more sandwiches
mixed with cutting board...

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.400
What's this?

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.500
Drink up.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:12.940
It's apple cider.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.870
It's made at the farm where we
usually get our apple juice.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:21.890
So these are related to
our calvados, right?

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.930
Huh?

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.400
Oh, I see... She found out.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.860
Huh?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.590
We can give these two
as gifts, right?

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:38.080
Eh? Yeah, that's true.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.140
Gifts?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.160
Phone Duty - Reserved
for Emergencies

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.150
Tonight, there's a merchant
guild's meeting.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:47.740
They help us out with a lot of things,
so from time to time, we give them presents.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:48.920
Keep that in mind.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:49.960
Okay!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:55.250
What? They tried their
hardest to hide it.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.990
How'd you find out?

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.710
W-Well, uh...

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.440
I'll tell you sometime, maybe.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.950
Would you like to eat
lunch with us?

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:12.820
What?

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.960
You want me to go, too?

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.700
Everyone wants a real explanation
from the military

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.550
about the news in this
week's papers.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:22.580
News?

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:26.250
About how the peace treaty conferences
aren't going well.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.250
They aren't?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:32.820
They're working out the reparations
and territorial lines.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.090
It's natural that it would drag on.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.340
Really, the old guild guys
want to see you.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.150
You've gained a lot more fans.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:45.090
Ever since you played a Flame Maiden
at the water-throwing festival,

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:47.520
their numbers have
been growing.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.860
What a pain...

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.770
So, yeah. I've gotta go to this.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:00.070
Now I'm a Fortress Maiden,
heart and soul, too!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.990
I will complete my mission!

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.030
All right. It's in your hands.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.000
Right!

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.730
Kanata, I'll give these to you.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.010
Sorry that they're so old.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.480
These are trumpet...

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:23.060
These are wonderful, wonderful,
wonderful!

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.720
Thank you!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.010
You're really sounding better
with the trumpet.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:30.040
They're a present for
practicing so hard.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.860
And they'll keep you awake.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.080
Ah... This is...

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:48.870
C... D... E... F... G...

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.690
A.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.040
I guess summer's over...

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.540
Iliya?

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.080
Maybe I drank too much.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.780
Noël-chan, are you there?

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:37.770
It's raining!

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.550
The laundry's gonna get wet!

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:45.390
The courtyard's within the
theater of operations!

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.270
Kanata!

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.020
Let's play!

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.570
Hello!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.620
Kanata!

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:01.900
Let's play!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.960
Save me!

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.920
Thank you so much.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:20.170
No, I'm glad your laundry is safe.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:26.750
Yeah... I-I'm sorry to
ask you for help!

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:28.350
Don't worry about it.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.640
I'm sorry for visiting so suddenly.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:36.800
I have to return to Treize tomorrow,
so I came to say goodbye.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.040
O-Oh, thank you.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.910
There's no need to say
goodbye to soldiers.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.270
Don't be like that, Seiya-san.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:49.410
I've heard he's been less than polite
to people from your base.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:54.230
I'd like to apologize
for that, as well.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.580
Where is everyone?

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.730
They're all gone.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:01.140
Rio-san, too? The black-haired one?

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.090
Yes.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.220
I see...

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.090
I'd like to see her...

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.100
Is this your book?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:10.600
What is it?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.130
A trumpet book.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.180
Rio-sempai gave it to me.

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:17.560
I see. I thought so.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.050
No, no. I'm sorry.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:23.070
Don't worry about it.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.130
Are you here alone?

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:26.130
That's right.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.070
I'm here for the uh...

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.820
command communications line...

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:36.570
for high-level HQ emergency situations...

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:37.790
So basically...

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:44.350
You're waiting for this to ring?

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:45.090
Yep!

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:50.370
But I've never used one
before, so I'm nervous.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:54.300
I'm not sure that I'll do it right.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.390
How about practicing?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.650
Then Yumina-san is also attending
the guild meeting?

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:09.940
Yes. She's going to get donations
from the guild.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.930
Here you go! Enjoy.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.470
Yummy!

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.920
Isn't it? You have some too, Seiya-kun.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.130
Fine, I'll drink your stupid cider.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.840
But don't think you can
buy me off with it!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.910
What are you making?

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.430
Can you two guess?

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:36.930
A phone!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.610
Is this really a phone?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.780
Yes, it's a phone!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:54.250
I make it for the kids,
'cause kids love phones.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.560
Go, Seiya-san.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.540
A phone, huh?

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.690
Hello?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.620
Hello?

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:07.490
Wow!

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.760
Wow, Seiya-kun!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.630
I can hear you!

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:11.840
That's not right.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.630
Say, "Hello," first.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.090
You always say that
on the phone.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.530
H-Hello?

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.390
Hello?

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:21.540
Wow!

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.490
I can really hear his voice!

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.170
Practice with that.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:27.690
OK!

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.770
Um... This is...

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:31.660
Hello?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.700
H-Hello!

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:40.280
This is Private Sorami Kanata of the
1121 Platoon, Helvetia Republic Army.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.710
Very well.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.710
I-I'm honored to receive
this phone call!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.890
Very well.

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.970
So, uh...

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.280
Wait, birdie!

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:54.050
Mishio-san!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.100
No, Mishio-chan!

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:00.680
What happened?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.950
<i>The phone!</i>

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:37.100
Um... Is the priest and our...

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.410
Yes?

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:04.620
Oh gods! How horrible!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:10.960
You came here to thank them for everything
they'd done and to say goodbye,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:14.110
but instead, you messed around
and caused trouble for them!

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.780
No dinner tonight!

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:18.150
Yes.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.560
Me, too?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.750
It's OK now.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.710
Thanks.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.280
But your clothes are soaked.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.280
I'm fine. I have a change...

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.780
I've got a good idea!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:47.180
This is embarrassing...

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.070
Not at all!

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.710
How brilliant you look!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.360
But thank you, Yumina-san!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.470
I'll wash and return them.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.220
No. You can keep them!

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.940
They're too big for the kids,

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:08.640
and I can't imagine anyone looking
as good as you in them!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.350
I'm sorry, Kanata.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:15.090
Will you play with us again?

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.000
Sure.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.810
Come back soon, Seiya-kun.

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:19.640
I...

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.120
M-Maybe if I'm free.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.950
Then excuse us.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:35.130
May all blessings be upon you.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.810
Th-Thank you!

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.400
Now, then. I need to clean up.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.040
I forgot.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.270
I have to go to the bathroom.

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.320
I'm gonna wet my pants...

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:18.810
Someone, hurry!

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.670
Hurry...

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:28.910
Geez, those old guys...

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.700
What's wrong, Kana-

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:34.100
Sempai, please...

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:36.940
Save me!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.920
What's wrong, Kanata?

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:41.420
I can't hold it anymore...

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.430
I'm gonna wet my pants!

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.210
Go, you'll get sick!

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.680
Thank you!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.890
She was holding it in
this whole time?

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.770
She'll really do whatever she's told.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.540
What's wrong?

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:08.030
I'm OK!

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:10.540
Kanata!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:15.200
No, I can't get it...
I can't move at all!

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:18.040
Man, her timing sucks.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.260
Hello?

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:26.730
This is Master Sergeant Rio Kazumiya of
the 1121 Platoon of the Helvetia Army.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.250
It's been a while.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.620
I heard we were confirming your line.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.180
So I insisted...

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:36.060
Are you going to run?

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.350
No!

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.790
I'm not running!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.960
I know.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:43.720
You simply haven't forgiven me.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:47.070
After all this time,
what do you want?

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:52.080
Please! I want you to save this
country... Save Helvetia.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:56.540
Morning, Kanata.

00:21:56.950 --> 00:22:01.300
Noël-chan, surely you haven't
been in there the whole day?

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.550
